  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): ASC 820-10-35-16A requires fair value measurements to reflect assumptions market participants would use, not entity-specific inputs. The 14% discount rate reflects the risk market participants assign to comparable intangible assets, yielding approximately $1,030,000 for $300,000 annually over 5 years.
Wrong (A): Using Silverline''s own 9% WACC violates ASC 820''s market participant principle by substituting entity-specific assumptions for market-based inputs.
Wrong (B): Averaging entity-specific and market rates has no basis in ASC 820; the standard requires market participant assumptions exclusively.
