-- Q11765: State and Local Government [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 68, paragraphs 33-36, differences between projected and actual earnings on plan investments are reported as deferred outflows (for losses) or deferred inflows (for gains) and amortized into pension expense over a closed five-year period. This smoothing prevents short-term market volatility from distorting pension expense.
Wrong (A): GASB 68 specifically prohibits immediate recognition of investment experience differences; the five-year amortization is mandatory.
Wrong (C): The investment shortfall does not directly reduce plan fiduciary net position by the full amount in one period; it is captured through the deferred outflow mechanism.
Wrong (D): GASB 68 does not permit deferring recognition until the next valuation; the loss is recorded as a deferred outflow in the period it occurs.$EXPL$
