  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB 34, paragraphs 23-25, governments may use the modified approach for eligible infrastructure assets if they maintain an asset management system with periodic condition assessments and preserve assets at or above an established condition level. Preservation costs are expensed rather than capitalized under this approach.
Wrong (A): Capitalizing preservation costs is incorrect under the modified approach; only additions and improvements that increase capacity or efficiency are capitalized.
Wrong (B): Infrastructure assets are not exempt from depreciation. Governments must either depreciate them or meet the modified approach requirements.
