  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB 34, governmental funds use the current financial resources measurement focus, so the $750,000 capital outlay is reported as an expenditure. In the government-wide statements using full accrual, the truck is capitalized and depreciated: $750,000 / 15 years x 10/12 months = $41,667 for the partial year.
Wrong (B): This reverses the correct treatment. Fund statements report expenditures for capital outlays, while government-wide statements capitalize assets.
Wrong (C): Governmental fund statements never report depreciation expense; depreciation appears only in government-wide statements under full accrual accounting.
Wrong (D): Government-wide statements require capitalization of capital assets, not expensing. Reporting $750,000 as an expense would violate accrual basis requirements.$EXPL$
